PART-01 — REPOSITORY REALITY ASSESSMENT
1. Purpose

The Repository Reality Assessment is the first implementation activity of Stage-24.

Its purpose is to establish the actual implementation baseline of the existing COREI repository before any repository modifications begin.

Unlike architecture reviews, this assessment evaluates implementation reality.

The repository—not documentation—is the implementation authority.

2. Mission

Determine the current implementation maturity of every engineering capability and identify how Stage-24 should evolve the existing platform.

The assessment answers one question:

"What is the current engineering reality of COREI?"

3. Philosophy

Implementation decisions shall be based upon repository evidence.

Not assumptions.

Not documentation.

Not memory.

Every engineering decision shall be supported by repository reality.

4. Assessment Scope

The Repository Reality Assessment covers the complete institutional engineering ecosystem.

Including:

repositories
directories
frameworks
shared engines
services
runtimes
UI
terminals
workspaces
contracts
schemas
governance
