These become the authoritative implementation planning artifacts.

17. Exit Criteria

The Engineering Gap Analysis is complete when:

every engineering capability has been assessed
every engineering gap has been classified
every implementation decision has been approved
engineering priorities have been assigned
implementation complexity has been evaluated
institutional risks have been identified
dependency impacts have been documented
the implementation backlog is fully defined

Completion of this part authorizes the transition from analysis to engineering execution planning, where implementation work packages and repository modifications are formally defined.

