21. Constraints

The following constraints apply after certification.

Phase-00A becomes frozen.
Phase-00B becomes frozen.
Engineering standards shall not be redefined.
Repository ownership shall remain unchanged unless governed.
Engineering workflows become institutional policy.
Toolchain decisions become institutional standards.
Future phases consume the Engineering Environment rather than extending it.
22. Phase-00 Closure Statement

Phase-00 is formally complete when:

the Institutional Engineering Environment has been specified
the implementation blueprint has been approved
repository evolution has been planned
engineering governance has been established
implementation sequencing has been frozen
work packages have been defined
engineering readiness has been certified

At this point, the COREI Engineering Environment ceases to be a planning initiative and becomes the permanent engineering foundation of the COREI platform.

From this point onward, Stage-24 transitions from engineering planning to repository implementation, beginning with Phase-01 — COREI Operating Environment.

